  "behavior_evidence": [
    "Shared operation engine commits the ordinary mutation, canonical receipt, task effect authority and journal in one transaction; injected late SQL failure rolls everything back.",
    "Matching task/step/logical ID reconciles without another mutation; different intent conflicts, and two tasks cannot alias an ordinary account receipt.",
    "Expired or revoked grants, revoked backing credentials and cancelled tasks deny accepted-effect replay; currently authorized owner inspection retains effect evidence.",
    "A real accepted Send question stays pending until its own attributed answer; another task reply cannot satisfy it. Agent-to-agent replies use the answering task authority.",
    "Messaging provider jobs retain pending/uncertain/failure distinctions; interrupted dispatch is not requeued by replay. Revocation or cancellation blocks task-linked queued messaging dispatch.",
    "CAS leases bound lifetime and installation concurrency; matching replay does not renew a lease, competing connections cannot both claim, and durable dispatch prevents reclamation.",
    "Actual child processes exit immediately before/after task commit for owner invocation, grant invocation and native recipient reply. Retry commits at most one logical message/effect/reply transition.",
    "Additive schema 11-to-12 upgrade preserves tasks/grants; conflicting schema migration rolls back. Legacy effects without protected dispatch metadata remain read-only."
  ],
  "review": {
